 ok←Book seat
⍝ Sell one seat. Returns 1 if this clerk claimed it, 0 if it was already taken.
⍝ TODO: this races two ways. Two clerks can double-book, because the check and the
⍝ claim are on separate lines; and the board tears, because SEATS and SOLD update on
⍝ separate lines.
 :If 0=SEATS[seat]           ⍝ CHECK: is the seat free?
     {}⎕DL 0.001             ⍝ another clerk may run here (widens the race)
     SEATS[seat]←1           ⍝ ACT: claim it …
     {}⎕DL 0.0003            ⍝ board is TORN here: SEATS updated, SOLD not yet
     SOLD+←1                 ⍝ … and bump the count on a LATER line
     ok←1
 :Else
     ok←0
 :EndIf
